  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 Arkansas Tech University Catalog, 'Fisheries and Wildlife Sciences Fisheries Option, Bachelor of Science' curriculum (pp. 360-362), a genuine institution-published semester sequence. The catalog prints 'Total Hours 120-119' (the sophomore-fall select-one slot floats: FW 3084 Ichthyology at 4 hours vs. a 3-hour statistics course); seeded here with the FW 3084 (4-hour) option for a total of 120, with the range documented. Footnote 2: 'Statistics must be taken either fall or spring term.' Footnote 4 (elective requirement): choose FW 3084 Ichthyology and FW 4024 Limnology; include at least two courses from the biology group (BIOL 3174 Physiological Ecology, BIOL 3034 Genetics, BIOL 4064 Evolutionary Biology, BIOL 3064 Parasitology, BIOL 3104 or AGPM 3104 Introduction to Entomology, BIOL 3184 Animal Behavior, BIOL 3004 Plant Taxonomy, BIOL 3033 Bioinformatics, BIOL 4043 Conservation Genetics, BIOL 4044 Dendrology, BIOL 4094 Coastal Ecology), one course from the physical science group (any physics course, AGSS 2014 Soils, GEOL 1014 Physical Geology), and three 3000-4000 level fisheries and wildlife electives; sufficient additional electives to reach 120 hours. Footnote 5: the 'Math' choice must include one of FW 3173 Biostatistics, MATH 2243 Calculus for Business and Economics, MATH 2914 Calculus I, MATH 2924 Calculus II, MATH 2934 Calculus III, STAT 2304 Programming Languages for Data Science, STAT 3113 Regression Analysis, STAT 4153 Experimental Design and Analysis. Footnote 6: this program partners the BS in Fisheries and Wildlife with the MS Fisheries and Wildlife — up to 12 graduate-level FW hours (four FW 5000/6000-level courses) can substitute for undergraduate FW requirements; noted here only, never seeded. One of the social sciences must be ECON 2003. Candidates complete comprehensive practical/technical exams for graduation; no more than 12 hours of 'D's may apply. Machine prereqs omitted (prereq: []) — the curriculum page prints no per-course prerequisites. tccns mirrors the local ATU course code; transfer_confidence core_only.",
